cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. For the method itself,
  cite the original papers listed under "references".
type: software
title: "NLM-FAD: Nonlinear Magnification (FAD), a TypeScript / WebGL2 port"
authors:
  - family-names: Keahey
    given-names: T. Alan
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ts232/nlm-fad"
url: "https://ts232.github.io/nlm-fad/"
abstract: >-
  A TypeScript / WebGL2 re-implementation of FAD, the author's nonlinear
  magnification (focus+context / fisheye) toolkit from his Indiana University
  PhD work (1995-1998; later the Magnivista SDK). Two engines: closed-form
  pipeline transformations, and magnification fields solved by an area-based
  diffusion relaxation of a mesh. Four standalone browser demos.
keywords:
  - nonlinear magnification
  - fisheye views
  - focus+context
  - detail-in-context
  - information visualization
  - mesh relaxation
  - WebGL2
